      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T00:55:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is loadEnvConfig alone responsible for an additional 1.4s of runtime? That\u0027s a strikingly long time to read a single file, and sounds like it might be low hanging fruit to improve all build times. Is it possible to carve out a quicker-running piece for upload-only?\n(I\u0027d also love to see an analysis, and a filed bug, for something that could offer a \u003e 1s savings on all builds)\n\nRegardless, your CL description and comments implied that this shortcut wasn\u0027t being made for performance reasons, but that it was a lack of understanding as to the root cause of a bug. Is that no longer the case? \n\nHow is ANDROID_ENABLE_METRICS_UPLOAD set? Is it always set? It seems to be set by rbesetup.sh, and that\u0027s unclear to me that it\u0027s guaranteed to be run.",
